      "content": "None"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The None keyword is used to indicate null i.e. no value."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1x = None\n2print(x)    # None"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As we know, a function can return a value. However, if we do not return a value, the function returns None. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "1def greet():\n2    print(\"Hey\")\n3\n4result = greet()\n5print(result)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Hey\nNone"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the greet() function doesn't return any value, which means it returns None."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
